      "future": "A distinct future schema gives E2/E3 separate once intents and predecessor links. E3 rebuilds E2 from its own seven saved inputs, exact same boot/owner/session/schema and complete nonuncertain result. A dedicated E2 qualifier must read its exact suffix/prefix-qualified operation delta and epoch2 stages, not replay the E1 parser over cumulative logs that still contain old E1 success. Missing, duplicate, mixed, out-of-order, interrupted or altered history admits diagnostics only. Save epoch intent/in-flight state before opening control. Never erase an intent to recover missing state.",
