  "future_sequence": [
    "Future fresh boot only: append current911ae710-78af-4702-8dfc-f4145decbd38 to all seven existing REFUSED_BOOTS. Apart from the required boot-ID read, reject a consumed boot before any live/candidate-content access. Require a distinct family/receipt/preparation/GNU identity and immutable per-epoch evidence, then all selected kernel/source/artifact pins, exact owned cold B20/reply, original owner identity, no work and one first management shutdown E1. Never retest/rebuild frozen v11 or clear a warmed intent.",
    "Run E2 once through the already evidenced management sequence. Preserve all E1/E2 intents and evidence; root freezes complete E2 raw captures and reconstructs its own seven-input OFF proof before any E3 command.",
    "For E3 require exact predecessor epoch2 and same boot/owner, complete uncertainty-free proof, unchanged cold AP20 provenance/original identity, no work and fresh PMGR OFF/held0/usage0/suspended/error0. No powered-off ASC/FIFO access.",
    "Consume the distinct E3 intent durably. Own one new PM get, verify strict ACTIVE/accounting and identity, fresh preON6a/6c, separate paired ON, fresh postON6a/6c/6d and fresh post-intent START RMW/readback. Preserve current stage-specific status admission; do not broaden it speculatively.",
    "Own fresh HELLO12 and both exact maps, fresh exact autonomous Running7/20, then guarded carried-AP20 skip with no B20/fallback/fresh reply. Keep the current empty retained application bitmap for this pure management comparison; native app-rollcall belongs to a separate designed variant. This bitmap alone does not prove actual firmware endpoints disabled.",
    "Own exactly one E3 management202 after fresh guards before and after its intent log. Accept only fresh EP0/type7/low8 in{1,2} within existing bounds; Running20 and cached E2 ACK cannot qualify. Preserve a separate bounded E3 receive journal.",
    "Require fresh RXempty/idle and checked CPUclear10/20 readbacks, own paired OFF and one E3 put, then strict physicalOFF/accounting/original identity/AP20 chain. Freeze E3 complete proof and independently compare E1/E2/E3 transcripts without rewriting any prior epoch.",
    "Every failure or unknown seals all remaining controls and retains all174 backing pages/root/context/maps/MMIO/module. After successful E3 there is no E4, cleanup, release or work path. Diagnostics expose last completed epoch and current fresh PMGR/accounting."
  ],
