  "next_dependency_comparison": {
    "repeatability": "One E3 on a future fresh candidate is the smallest additional hardware question for the explicit repeatable-teardown objective. It isolates repeated management state and per-epoch ownership; two successes would still be bounded evidence, not general reset/recovery.",
    "execution": "The more direct execution gap is native retained endpoint rollcall plus fresh observable application/control progress and UAT/context readiness. A second management restart with an empty application bitmap does not resolve those. Continue their offline native/FW audit in parallel; E3 is not a logical prerequisite for that audit or for a separate fresh-boot application rejoin design.",
    "recommendation": "Prepare bounded E3 design and application-rejoin evidence independently, then choose the next hardware candidate from the concrete dependency being tested. Do not combine new rollcall/application publication with a pure management-repeatability claim or postpone execution indefinitely for more unchanged shutdown trials."
  },
